1
00:00:02,336 --> 00:00:03,545
HEY.

2
00:00:03,587 --> 00:00:05,506
HEY, CHECK IT OUT.
THIS IS UNBELIEVABLE.

3
00:00:05,547 --> 00:00:07,132
JOEY HAS BEEN
HOLDING HIS BREATH

4
00:00:07,174 --> 00:00:08,425
FOR ALMOST FOUR MINUTES.

5
00:00:13,848 --> 00:00:15,808
DUDE, ARE YOU TRYING TO KILL ME?

6
00:00:15,850 --> 00:00:17,309
PHEEBS.

7
00:00:17,351 --> 00:00:18,978
I WANT TO ASK YOU SOMETHING.

8
00:00:19,019 --> 00:00:19,979
UH-HUH. WHAT?

9
00:00:20,020 --> 00:00:21,563
WELL, SINCE
I'M MOVING OUT

10
00:00:21,605 --> 00:00:23,273
AN-AND YOU'RE
SO BEAUTIFUL..

11
00:00:23,315 --> 00:00:24,274
OH...
HOW ABOUT

12
00:00:24,316 --> 00:00:25,651
I MOVE IN WITH YOU?

13
00:00:25,693 --> 00:00:27,068
WELL, THAT WOULD BE GREAT

14
00:00:27,110 --> 00:00:29,237
BUT THEN WHAT DO WE DO
ABOUT DENISE?

15
00:00:30,447 --> 00:00:31,239
WHO'S DENISE?

16
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:32,407
MY ROOMMATE.

17
00:00:32,449 --> 00:00:33,492
DO YOU HAVE A ROOMMATE?

18
00:00:33,534 --> 00:00:35,828
YES, DENISE. DENISE.

19
00:00:37,371 --> 00:00:39,247
WHAT IS WITH
THE SECRECY, PHOEBE?

20
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:40,875
AND WHAT ABOUT THIS DENISE?

21
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:42,083
IS SHE CUTE?

22
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,919
PHEEBS, I DON'T
UNDERSTAND.

23
00:00:43,961 --> 00:00:46,087
HOW CAN YOU HAVE A ROOMMATE
NONE OF US KNOW ABOUT?

24
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:48,465
MAYBE BECAUSE YOU NEVER LISTEN
TO ANYTHING THAT I SAY.

25
00:00:48,507 --> 00:00:49,884
I TALK ABOUT HER ALL THE TIME.

26
00:00:49,925 --> 00:00:50,968
DENISE!

27
00:00:51,010 --> 00:00:53,094
Joey:
HEY, RACHE, LISTEN...

28
00:00:53,136 --> 00:00:54,889
I WAS THINKING, UH,
I'M GOING TO HAVE

29
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:56,431
AN EXTRA ROOM
OVER AT MY PLACE.

30
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,599
OH, THAT'S TRUE.

31
00:00:57,641 --> 00:00:59,309
YEAH, WHY DON'T YOU
MOVE IN WITH ME?

32
00:00:59,351 --> 00:01:02,270
WE CAN, LIKE, STAY UP
LATE TALKING AND WATCH MOVIES...

33
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:04,565
AND YOU KNOW
ABOUT NAKED THURSDAYS, RIGHT?

34
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:09,820
YEAH, YEAH, I THINK I'M
GOING TO FIND MY OWN PLACE.

35
00:01:09,862 --> 00:01:10,905
HEY, HEY!

36
00:01:10,946 --> 00:01:12,322
I THOUGHT NAKED THURSDAYS

37
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:13,741
WAS JUST OUR THING, MAN.

38
00:01:21,040 --> 00:01:26,336
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

39
00:01:26,378 --> 00:01:28,547
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

40
00:01:28,589 --> 00:01:30,841
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

41
00:01:30,883 --> 00:01:35,846
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

42
00:01:35,888 --> 00:01:38,057
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

43
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:40,308
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

44
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:44,605
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

45
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:50,569
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

46
00:01:55,407 --> 00:01:56,408
HEY.

47
00:01:56,450 --> 00:01:57,743
HI.

48
00:01:57,785 --> 00:01:59,160
SO WHAT DID
RACHEL SAY

49
00:01:59,202 --> 00:02:01,080
WHEN YOU TOLD HER YOU
WERE STILL MARRIED TO HER?

50
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:02,247
OH, THAT. UM...

51
00:02:02,289 --> 00:02:04,416
SHE TOOK IT REALLY WELL.

52
00:02:04,458 --> 00:02:05,834
OH. YOU DIDN'T TELL
HER, DID YOU?

53
00:02:05,876 --> 00:02:07,669
NO.

54
00:02:07,711 --> 00:02:09,797
OF COURSE NOT, BECAUSE
YOU'RE IN LOVE WITH HER.

55
00:02:09,838 --> 00:02:11,090
I AM NOT IN
LOVE WITH HER.

56
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:12,466
SHE WAS VERY UPSET

57
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:14,676
ABOUT HAVING TO MOVE OUT
SO I-I DIDN'T TELL HER

58
00:02:14,718 --> 00:02:15,803
WE WERE STILL MARRIED

59
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,429
'CAUSE SHE'D ONLY
GET MORE UPSET.

60
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:18,806
I-I-I JUST, I
COMFORTED HER

61
00:02:18,847 --> 00:02:19,974
AS A FRIEND.

62
00:02:20,015 --> 00:02:21,516
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
COMFORTED HER?

63
00:02:21,558 --> 00:02:23,351
IT WAS NOTHING,
JUST GAVE HER A HUG.

64
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:26,438
UH-HUH! A CLASSIC
SIGN OF LOVE, THE HUG.

65
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:29,149
IT'S ALSO A SIGN
OF FRIENDSHIP.

66
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,359
YEAH, NOT IN YOUR CASE,
LOVEY LOVERSON.

67
00:02:32,945 --> 00:02:34,071
IT WAS A HUG.

68
00:02:34,113 --> 00:02:35,405
ALL RIGHT, JUST
TELL ME THIS.

69
00:02:35,447 --> 00:02:37,198
DID YOU OR DID YOU NOT
SMELL HER HAIR?

70
00:02:37,240 --> 00:02:39,367
S-SM-SMELL HER HAIR?

71
00:02:39,409 --> 00:02:41,578
WELL, WHAT IF I DID?

72
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:45,457
90% OF A WOMAN'S PHEROMONES
COME OUT THE TOP OF HER HEAD.

73
00:02:45,499 --> 00:02:48,251
THAT'S WHY,
THAT'S WHY WOMEN ARE SHORTER.

74
00:02:48,293 --> 00:02:51,588
SO THAT MEN WILL FALL
IN LOVE WHEN THEY HUG THEM.

75
00:02:51,630 --> 00:02:54,257
OH, COME ON, ROSS,
YOU'RE A SCIENTIST.

76
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:57,594
I WAS HUGGING HER
AS A FRIEND, OKAY.

77
00:02:57,636 --> 00:03:00,388
IT'S NOT MY FAULT HER,
HER HAIR GOT IN MY FACE.

78
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:01,682
SHE'S GOT A LOT OF IT

79
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:03,433
AND IT SMELLS
ALL, ALL, UH...

80
00:03:03,475 --> 00:03:05,226
( inhales )

81
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:06,728
YOU KNOW, COCONUTTY.

82
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,815
WHAT? OH--

83
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:12,191
THAT DOESN'T MEAN I
HAVE FEELINGS FOR RACHEL.

84
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:14,653
MAYBE IT MEANS I HAVE
FEELINGS FOR COCONUTS.

85
00:03:14,695 --> 00:03:15,904
OKAY. WHATEVER YOU SAY

86
00:03:15,946 --> 00:03:17,572
BUT JUST BE CAREFUL,
ALL RIGHT?

87
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,700
RACHEL'S NOT
IN THE SAME PLACE YOU ARE.

88
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:21,785
OKAY, IF THE PLACE
YOU'RE REFERRING TO

89
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:23,120
IS BEING IN LOVE

90
00:03:23,162 --> 00:03:25,998
THEN SHE IS IN THE
SAME PLACE AS ME

91
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:28,542
BECAUSE I AM NOT
IN THAT PLACE.

92
00:03:28,583 --> 00:03:30,919
OKAY, I DIDN'T
UNDERSTAND THAT

93
00:03:30,961 --> 00:03:32,337
BUT, YOU KNOW

94
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:34,422
MAYBE THAT'S 'CAUSE
YOU WERE SPEAKING

95
00:03:34,464 --> 00:03:36,091
THE SECRET LANGUAGE OF LOVE.

96
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:41,596
HEY.
HI.

97
00:03:41,638 --> 00:03:43,264
DUDE, SOME GUY
JUST CALLED FOR YOU.

98
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:44,058
WHO WAS IT?

99
00:03:44,099 --> 00:03:45,559
I DON'T KNOW.

100
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:48,311
HOW ABOUT, "THANKS
FOR TAKING THE MESSAGE"? GEEZ.

101
00:03:48,353 --> 00:03:50,438
HEY, LISTEN,
YOU KNOW

102
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,191
WHEN YOU MOVE IN,
RACHEL'S ROOM'S

103
00:03:52,232 --> 00:03:53,316
GOING TO BE EMPTY.

104
00:03:53,358 --> 00:03:54,484
YOU WANT
TO TALK ABOUT

105
00:03:54,526 --> 00:03:55,944
WHAT WE WANT
TO DO WITH IT?

106
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:57,071
SURE.

107
00:03:57,112 --> 00:03:58,613
OKAY. I WAS THINKING
WE SHOULD HAVE

108
00:03:58,655 --> 00:04:00,032
A BEAUTIFUL
GUEST ROOM, RIGHT?

109
00:04:00,074 --> 00:04:01,491
WITH A MAHOGANY SLEIGH BED

110
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:03,702
AND BEDSIDE TABLES
WITH FLOWERS ON IT ALL THE TIME

111
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:04,995
AND THEN WE CAN HAVE

112
00:04:05,037 --> 00:04:06,663
A ROLL-TOP DESK
WITH LITTLE COMMENT CARDS

113
00:04:06,705 --> 00:04:08,165
SO PEOPLE
CAN TELL US HOW MUCH

114
00:04:08,207 --> 00:04:09,583
THEY LOVED
STAYING HERE.

115
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:10,792
OR WHATEVER, YOU KNOW.

116
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:12,544
I REALLY HAVEN'T THOUGHT
ABOUT IT MUCH.

117
00:04:12,586 --> 00:04:16,173
WELL, I LIKE THAT
IDEA. OBVIOUSLY.

118
00:04:16,215 --> 00:04:19,300
BUT I WAS THINKING MAYBE,
MAYBE... MAYBE IT COULD BE

119
00:04:19,342 --> 00:04:20,677
A GAME ROOM, YOU KNOW.

120
00:04:20,719 --> 00:04:22,846
I MEAN, YOU CAN BUY
OLD ARCADE GAMES

121
00:04:22,888 --> 00:04:26,016
LIKE, UH, LIKE SPACE INVADERS
AND ASTEROIDS FOR $200.

122
00:04:26,058 --> 00:04:28,351
THE REAL ONES,
THE BIG, BIG, BIG ONES.

123
00:04:29,937 --> 00:04:31,021
NO.

124
00:04:31,063 --> 00:04:32,522
OKAY, SO YOU MEAN "NO"

125
00:04:32,564 --> 00:04:36,026
AS IN, "GEE, CHANDLER,
WHAT AN INTERESTING IDEA

126
00:04:36,068 --> 00:04:39,696
LET'S DISCUSS IT BEFORE
WE REJECT IT COMPLETELY."

127
00:04:39,738 --> 00:04:42,074
OH, I'M SORRY. OF COURSE.

128
00:04:43,575 --> 00:04:45,035
YES, INTERESTING IDEA.

129
00:04:45,077 --> 00:04:46,745
TALK ABOUT IT, BUT... NO.

130
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:49,539
SO THAT'S IT?

131
00:04:49,581 --> 00:04:51,792
I JUST DON'T THINK THAT,
YOU KNOW, ARCADE GAMES

132
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,376
GO IN THE BEAUTIFUL GUEST ROOM.

133
00:04:53,418 --> 00:04:54,461
THE BEAUTIFUL
GUEST ROOM'S

134
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:55,879
GOING TO BE FILLED
WITH ANTIQUES.

135
00:04:55,921 --> 00:04:58,173
WHICH IS WHY
ASTEROIDS IS PERFECT.

136
00:04:58,215 --> 00:04:59,716
IT'S THE OLDEST GAME.

137
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:03,344
WHAT DO YOU HAVE AGAINST
THE BEAUTIFUL GUEST ROOM?

138
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:06,347
NOTHING. I DON'T HAVE ANYTHING
AGAINST THE BEAUTIFUL GUEST ROOM

139
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:08,183
ESPECIALLY SINCE
EVERYBODY THAT WE KNOW

140
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:09,601
LIVES ABOUT 30 SECONDS AWAY.

141
00:05:10,602 --> 00:05:12,062
ARE YOU MOCKING ME?

142
00:05:12,104 --> 00:05:13,188
NO, I'M NOT MOCKING YOU

143
00:05:13,230 --> 00:05:14,773
OR YOUR "BEAUTIFUL GUEST ROOM."

144
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:21,280
HEY, WHAT'S UP?

145
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:24,158
OH, NOTHING. MONICA AND
I HAD A STUPID FIGHT.

146
00:05:24,199 --> 00:05:26,285
BUT YOU'RE STILL MOVING IN
TOGETHER, RIGHT?

147
00:05:26,325 --> 00:05:27,786
'CAUSE MY AD CAME OUT TODAY.

148
00:05:28,954 --> 00:05:32,291
"WANTED, FEMALE ROOMMATE,
NONSMOKER, NON-UGLY."

149
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:35,460
NICE.

150
00:05:35,502 --> 00:05:36,628
YEAH?

151
00:05:36,670 --> 00:05:38,297
I JUST FIGURED
AFTER LIVING WITH YOU

152
00:05:38,337 --> 00:05:40,257
IT WOULD BE AN INTERESTING
CHANGE OF PACE

153
00:05:40,299 --> 00:05:41,633
TO HAVE
A FEMALE ROOMMATE.

154
00:05:41,675 --> 00:05:43,802
YOU KNOW? SOMEONE
I COULD LEARN FROM.

155
00:05:43,844 --> 00:05:46,554
SOMEONE...
SOMEONE WHO'S DIFFERENT THAN ME

156
00:05:46,596 --> 00:05:49,975
AND WHAT'S MORE DIFFERENT
THAN ME-- A GUY WHO'S NOT 19--

157
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:51,852
THAN, SAY, A GIRL WHO IS 19?

158
00:05:51,893 --> 00:05:53,478
YEAH?

159
00:05:53,520 --> 00:05:55,814
NOT JUST A HAT RACK, MY FRIEND.

160
00:05:57,899 --> 00:05:59,943
PHEEBS, I HAVE
TO ASK YOU...

161
00:05:59,985 --> 00:06:02,279
SHH! I'M SWAMPED RIGHT NOW.

162
00:06:02,321 --> 00:06:04,948
YOU'RE JUST
STARING INTO SPACE.

163
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:07,993
UM, I'M TRYING
TO MOVE THAT PENCIL.

164
00:06:08,035 --> 00:06:09,786
THIS ONE?

165
00:06:09,828 --> 00:06:12,413
IT WORKED!

166
00:06:12,455 --> 00:06:15,416
PHEEBS. THIS WHOLE
APARTMENT THING

167
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:16,793
IS A NIGHTMARE.

168
00:06:16,835 --> 00:06:18,170
EVERY PLACE THAT
I CAN AFFORD

169
00:06:18,212 --> 00:06:20,005
COMES WITH A ROOMMATE
WHO IS A FREAK.

170
00:06:20,047 --> 00:06:21,422
I MEAN, LOOK AT THIS.

171
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:26,469
"WANTED. FEMALE ROOMMATE.
NONSMOKER, NON-UGLY."

172
00:06:26,511 --> 00:06:29,139
I MEAN, IT'S JUST
THAT THERE'S NOTHING.

173
00:06:29,181 --> 00:06:30,807
THIS CITY IS FULL.

174
00:06:30,849 --> 00:06:32,976
WAIT, NO,
LOOK AT THIS.

175
00:06:33,018 --> 00:06:36,521
"TWO BEDROOM, TWO BATH,
MUST BE NONSMOKER.

176
00:06:36,563 --> 00:06:38,439
SATAN WORSHIPERS OKAY."

177
00:06:38,481 --> 00:06:41,735
OH, YEAH, BUT
IT'S ON THE GROUND FLOOR.

178
00:06:43,402 --> 00:06:44,363
HEY.

179
00:06:44,403 --> 00:06:45,613
HEY.

180
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:47,908
RACHE, UH, YOU STILL
LOOKING FOR A PLACE?

181
00:06:47,949 --> 00:06:48,950
YEAH, WHY?

182
00:06:48,992 --> 00:06:50,577
OKAY, THERE'S THIS GUY, WARREN

183
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:53,247
FROM THE MUSEUM AND HE'S GOING
ON A DIG FOR LIKE TWO YEARS

184
00:06:53,288 --> 00:06:55,082
AND HE'S GOT
THIS GREAT PLACE

185
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:57,834
HE NEEDS TO SUBLET,
SO, UH... YOU INTERESTED?

186
00:06:57,876 --> 00:06:58,877
THAT SOUNDS GREAT.

187
00:06:58,919 --> 00:07:00,379
I'D LOVE TO LIVE AT WARREN'S.

188
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:01,420
I LOVE WARREN.

189
00:07:01,462 --> 00:07:02,672
THANK YOU.

190
00:07:02,714 --> 00:07:04,174
DON'T THANK ME.

191
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:06,134
YOU WANT TO THANK SOMEONE,
THANK THE VOLCANO

192
00:07:06,176 --> 00:07:07,928
THAT ERUPTED THOUSANDS
OF YEARS AGO

193
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:10,013
KILLING,
BUT PERFECTLY PRESERVING

194
00:07:10,055 --> 00:07:12,057
AN ENTIRE
CIVILIZATION.

195
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:15,102
HERE'S WARREN'S NUMBER.

196
00:07:15,143 --> 00:07:16,561
OH, THIS IS GREAT.

197
00:07:16,603 --> 00:07:19,189
I AM GOING TO CALL HIM
RIGHT NOW!

198
00:07:19,231 --> 00:07:20,565
THANK YOU.

199
00:07:22,442 --> 00:07:24,027
OKAY.

200
00:07:24,069 --> 00:07:26,029
YOU GO CALL HIM.

201
00:07:26,071 --> 00:07:28,282
I SAW IT.

202
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:32,160
I DON'T KNOW WHAT
YOU'RE TALKING ABOUT.

203
00:07:32,202 --> 00:07:33,453
UM, I'M TALKING ABOUT THAT

204
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:35,122
WHICH YOU ALREADY KNOW
BUT WON'T ADMIT.

205
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,706
YOU KNOW,
THAT YOU LOVE HER AGAIN.

206
00:07:36,748 --> 00:07:37,999
YOU RE-LOVE HER.

207
00:07:38,041 --> 00:07:40,877
LOOK, I DO NOT RE-LOVE HER.

208
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:43,630
I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU WON'T JUST ADMIT IT.

209
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:47,550
OKAY, JUST PROMISE ME THAT
YOU WON'T DO ANYTHING STUPID.

210
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:49,677
LOOK, WE'RE JUST
FRIENDS NOW, OKAY?

211
00:07:49,719 --> 00:07:51,679
WHY WOULD I DO ANYTHING STUPID?

212
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:53,140
( growling )

213
00:07:53,181 --> 00:07:54,933
WELL, THE APARTMENT
IS ALREADY SUBLETTED.

214
00:07:54,975 --> 00:07:56,226
THIS IS JUST HOPELESS.

215
00:07:56,268 --> 00:07:58,145
I'M NEVER GOING
TO FIND ANYTHING.

216
00:07:58,186 --> 00:07:59,896
YOU CAN LIVE WITH ME.

217
00:07:59,938 --> 00:08:00,730
WHAT?

218
00:08:00,772 --> 00:08:01,273
WHAT?

219
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:04,525
WHAT?

220
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:09,781
OH, MY GOD

221
00:08:09,823 --> 00:08:11,032
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

222
00:08:12,451 --> 00:08:14,244
I WOULD LOVE TO LIVE
WITH YOU, ROSS.

223
00:08:14,286 --> 00:08:16,413
TH-THAT'S GREAT. THANK YOU.

224
00:08:16,455 --> 00:08:18,999
I-I'M JUST GLAD I COULD,
YOU KNOW, HELP YOU OUT.

225
00:08:20,083 --> 00:08:23,128
WOW, I'M,
I'M SO HAPPY FOR YOU GUYS.

226
00:08:23,170 --> 00:08:25,505
THIS IS SO, SO NOT STUPID.

227
00:08:28,091 --> 00:08:30,677
ROSS, ROSS, YOU HAVE
NO IDEA WHAT THIS MEANS TO ME

228
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,846
I MEAN, I MEAN
I WAS GOING TO BE HOMELESS.

229
00:08:32,887 --> 00:08:33,972
YOU'VE JUST SAVED ME.

230
00:08:34,014 --> 00:08:35,140
YOU'RE MY HERO.

231
00:08:35,182 --> 00:08:37,392
HERO. I, I DON'T KNOW.

232
00:08:37,434 --> 00:08:39,144
WELL, ALL RIGHT.

233
00:08:40,645 --> 00:08:42,397
OH, I HAVE TO GO
TELL MONICA

234
00:08:42,439 --> 00:08:44,524
WHAT A WONDERFUL
BROTHER SHE HAS.

235
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,151
OH, PLEASE...

236
00:08:52,949 --> 00:08:56,577
YOU'RE GOING TO SAY THINGS
NOW, AREN'T YOU?

237
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,205
NO. NO, I WON'T

238
00:08:58,246 --> 00:09:01,082
BUT I SHOULD TELL YOU THIS:

239
00:09:01,124 --> 00:09:04,585
THIS EXACT SAME THING
HAPPENED TO MY ROOMMATE DENISE.

240
00:09:04,627 --> 00:09:07,130
SHE MOVED IN WITH A GUY
WHO WAS SECRETLY MARRIED TO HER

241
00:09:07,172 --> 00:09:09,590
AND HE SAID HE DIDN'T LOVE HER
BUT HE REALLY DID

242
00:09:09,632 --> 00:09:11,009
AND IT JUST BLEW UP

243
00:09:11,051 --> 00:09:12,927
AND THAT'S HOW SHE ENDED UP
LIVING WITH ME.

244
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:18,808
OKAY, THAT'S A LIE.

245
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:23,188
HI.

246
00:09:23,230 --> 00:09:24,647
HI.

247
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:26,107
HI, LISTEN, I'M SORRY
ABOUT BEFORE.

248
00:09:26,149 --> 00:09:27,567
I DON'T NEED TO HAVE
A GAME ROOM.

249
00:09:27,608 --> 00:09:29,736
I MEAN, WHEN I WAS A KID
I ONLY PLAYED THOSE GAMES

250
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:30,945
BECAUSE I COULDN'T
GET GIRLS

251
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:31,988
AND NOW I
CAN GET 'EM.

252
00:09:33,281 --> 00:09:35,033
NOW I HAVE YOU.

253
00:09:36,535 --> 00:09:39,079
NO,-N-NOT THAT I THINK
I HAVE YOU...

254
00:09:39,120 --> 00:09:42,457
OR THINK OF YOU AS PROPERTY
IN ANY SORT OF WAY.

255
00:09:42,499 --> 00:09:43,458
I SEE WOMEN...

256
00:09:43,500 --> 00:09:44,376
STOP IT, CHANDLER.

257
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:47,754
I'M SORRY, TOO.

258
00:09:47,795 --> 00:09:49,047
REALLY?

259
00:09:49,089 --> 00:09:51,132
YEAH. OH, YES...

260
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:52,800
LISTEN, WE
DON'T HAVE

261
00:09:52,842 --> 00:09:53,968
TO MAKE THAT
A GUEST ROOM.

262
00:09:54,010 --> 00:09:55,136
WE CAN THINK
OF SOMETHING

263
00:09:55,178 --> 00:09:56,471
TO DO WITH THE
ROOM TOGETHER.

264
00:09:56,513 --> 00:09:57,556
THAT'S A GREAT IDEA.

265
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:59,057
WE CAN EASILY
THINK OF A WAY

266
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:00,683
FOR US BOTH
TO ENJOY THE ROOM.

267
00:10:00,725 --> 00:10:01,935
TOTALLY.

268
00:10:06,064 --> 00:10:07,232
WE DON'T HAVE

269
00:10:07,274 --> 00:10:08,525
TO COME UP
WITH THIS NOW.

270
00:10:08,567 --> 00:10:10,485
OH, GOOD.

271
00:10:10,527 --> 00:10:12,070
HEY, WHY DON'T WE
THINK ABOUT CHANGES

272
00:10:12,112 --> 00:10:13,488
WE CAN MAKE
IN THE LIVING ROOM.

273
00:10:13,530 --> 00:10:14,989
CHANGES?

274
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,824
YEAH, I MEAN,
WE'RE GOING TO HAVE

275
00:10:16,866 --> 00:10:18,452
TO MOVE AROUND
SOME FURNITURE

276
00:10:18,493 --> 00:10:19,953
TO MAKE ROOM
FOR MY CHAIR.

277
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:24,458
Y-Y-YOU'RE GOING TO BRING
THE BARCALOUNGER OVER HERE?

278
00:10:24,499 --> 00:10:26,167
IS THAT A PROBLEM?

279
00:10:26,209 --> 00:10:28,002
WELL... IT'S JUST
THAT THEY'RE A SET

280
00:10:28,044 --> 00:10:30,046
AND THEY SHOULD PROBABLY
STAY TOGETHER.

281
00:10:30,088 --> 00:10:31,506
OH, THAT'S COOL.

282
00:10:31,548 --> 00:10:33,592
THEN I'LL JUST, UH,
BRING THEM BOTH OVER.

283
00:10:33,632 --> 00:10:38,012
SEE, NOW, NOW, YOU'RE TAKING
THEM AWAY FROM THEIR HOME.

284
00:10:38,054 --> 00:10:39,013
OKAY. I GET IT.

285
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,014
SO I GET NOTHING.

286
00:10:40,056 --> 00:10:41,015
NOTHING HERE IS MINE.

287
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:42,100
EVERYTHING IS YOURS.

288
00:10:42,142 --> 00:10:43,560
I'LL GET UP IN THE MORNING

289
00:10:43,602 --> 00:10:45,770
PUT ON YOUR CLOTHES,
AND HEAD OFF TO WORK.

290
00:10:45,812 --> 00:10:47,063
YEAH, YEAH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

291
00:10:47,105 --> 00:10:48,731
YEAH, THAT'S IT--
EVERYTHING WILL BE MINE.

292
00:10:48,773 --> 00:10:49,732
NOTHING WILL BE YOURS.

293
00:10:49,774 --> 00:10:51,067
THAT'S WHAT I SAID.

294
00:10:51,109 --> 00:10:53,153
COME ON, I'M TALKING
ABOUT THE BARCALOUNGER!

295
00:10:53,194 --> 00:10:54,362
IT JUST, IT DOESN'T MATCH.

296
00:10:54,404 --> 00:10:55,489
WHERE IS IT GOING TO GO?

297
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:57,365
IN THE GAME ROOM!

298
00:10:57,407 --> 00:10:58,741
LOOK, IT IS NOT MY FAULT

299
00:10:58,783 --> 00:11:00,868
THAT YOUR CHAIRS
ARE INCREDIBLY UGLY.

300
00:11:00,910 --> 00:11:02,621
ALL RIGHT, THAT'S
FINE. THAT'S FINE.

301
00:11:02,661 --> 00:11:03,871
I WON'T BRING
THE CHAIRS.

302
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:05,123
I WON'T BRING
ANYTHING.

303
00:11:05,165 --> 00:11:07,167
I WOULDN'T WANT
TO RUIN THE AMBIANCE

304
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:08,960
OVER HERE AT GRANDMA'S PLACE!

305
00:11:10,086 --> 00:11:11,754
EVERYTHING ON
YOUR APPLICATION

306
00:11:11,796 --> 00:11:13,214
LOOKS REALLY GOOD. UH...

307
00:11:13,256 --> 00:11:14,757
OH, JUST ONE LAST QUESTION.
UH...

308
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:16,717
ARE YOU AND YOUR FRIENDS
GOING TO BE OVER HERE

309
00:11:16,759 --> 00:11:18,677
ALL THE TIME LIKE PARTYING
AND HANGING OUT?

310
00:11:18,719 --> 00:11:20,721
OH, DON'T WORRY,
I'M NOT REALLY A PARTY GIRL.

311
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:23,350
WHOA. NOW, LOOK.

312
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:25,726
DON'T JUST BE
BLURTING STUFF OUT.

313
00:11:25,768 --> 00:11:28,980
I WANT YOU TO REALLY
THINK ABOUT YOUR ANSWERS.

314
00:11:29,022 --> 00:11:30,315
( door opening )

315
00:11:30,357 --> 00:11:32,859
YOU CAN CALL OFF
THE ROOMMATE SEARCH.

316
00:11:32,900 --> 00:11:34,653
HI. I'LL BE LIVING HERE.

317
00:11:34,693 --> 00:11:36,196
DON'T LISTEN TO HIM.

318
00:11:36,237 --> 00:11:38,823
HE'S JUST SOME GUY WHO
REALLY WANTS THE APARTMENT

319
00:11:38,865 --> 00:11:40,908
BUT I DON'T THINK
HE'S GOING TO GET IT.

320
00:11:40,950 --> 00:11:43,161
WHY DID YOU TAKE THE
SHOWER CURTAIN DOWN?

321
00:11:43,203 --> 00:11:45,580
THAT THING WAS A HAZARD.

322
00:11:45,622 --> 00:11:48,416
I'M VERY SAFETY-CONSCIOUS.

323
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:57,842
HEY.

324
00:11:57,884 --> 00:11:59,302
HEY.

325
00:11:59,344 --> 00:12:01,596
OH, I WAS JUST CLEARING
SOME SPACE FOR YOUR STUFF.

326
00:12:01,638 --> 00:12:02,805
OH, THANKS.

327
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,432
BUT, LISTEN,
I WAS JUST AT MONICA'S

328
00:12:04,474 --> 00:12:06,267
AND SHE AND CHANDLER
HAD A BIG FIGHT

329
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:07,726
AND THEY'RE NOT MOVING IN.

330
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:10,104
WHAT DO YOU MEAN,
THEY'RE NOT MOVING IN?

331
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:12,399
THEY'RE-THEY'RE
STILL MOVING IN, RIGHT?

332
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,609
NO, NO. THEY JUST HAD
A BIG BLOWOUT

333
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:16,695
OVER WHAT TO DO WITH MY ROOM.

334
00:12:16,735 --> 00:12:19,489
WHAT? OVER A STUPID ROOM?

335
00:12:19,531 --> 00:12:21,032
I KNOW.
I FEEL KIND OF BAD FOR THEM

336
00:12:21,074 --> 00:12:22,367
BUT I'M ALSO REALLY PSYCHED

337
00:12:22,409 --> 00:12:24,160
'CAUSE NOW I DON'T HAVE
TO MOVE IN HERE.

338
00:12:24,202 --> 00:12:25,579
OH. NO-NO, YEAH.

339
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,121
NO, THAT PART'S GREAT.

340
00:12:28,456 --> 00:12:31,459
WHAT'S ALL THIS
ABOUT YOU GUYS FIGHTING?

341
00:12:32,877 --> 00:12:35,422
IS THIS REALLY OVER A ROOM?

342
00:12:35,463 --> 00:12:38,132
I MEAN, THAT IS SO SILLY.

343
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:40,843
ROSS, WE CAN HANDLE THIS.

344
00:12:40,885 --> 00:12:42,761
UH, APPARENTLY NOT

345
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:46,349
AND I CAN'T JUST STAND BY
AND WATCH TWO PEOPLE

346
00:12:46,391 --> 00:12:51,438
I CARE ABOUT SO MUCH BE HURT
BY SOMETHING THAT IS SO SILLY.

347
00:12:52,439 --> 00:12:53,565
I MEAN

348
00:12:53,607 --> 00:12:55,316
ENOUGH OF THE SILLINESS.

349
00:12:55,358 --> 00:12:56,775
WELL, WHY DON'T YOU

350
00:12:56,817 --> 00:12:58,486
TELL HER TO STOP BEING SILLY?

351
00:12:58,528 --> 00:13:00,154
( babbling )

352
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,073
ALL RIGHT, OKAY, OKAY.

353
00:13:04,367 --> 00:13:06,202
TWO VERY GOOD POINTS.

354
00:13:07,912 --> 00:13:11,332
LOOK... I'VE KNOWN YOU BOTH
A LONG TIME

355
00:13:11,374 --> 00:13:14,377
AND I'VE NEVER SEEN
EITHER OF YOU ONE-MILLIONTH

356
00:13:14,419 --> 00:13:17,631
AS HAPPY AS YOU'VE BEEN
SINCE YOU GOT TOGETHER.

357
00:13:17,672 --> 00:13:19,633
DO YOU REALLY WANT TO THROW

358
00:13:19,674 --> 00:13:22,510
THAT ALL AWAY OVER A ROOM?

359
00:13:22,552 --> 00:13:25,263
THAT IS SO SILLY.

360
00:13:25,305 --> 00:13:27,390
I MEAN, WHAT'S MORE IMPORTANT--

361
00:13:27,432 --> 00:13:30,518
LOVE... OR SILLINESS?

362
00:13:32,061 --> 00:13:34,897
WELL, WE ARE FOND
OF THE SILLINESS

363
00:13:34,939 --> 00:13:37,609
BUT WE ALSO HAVE
A SOFT SPOT FOR THE LOVE.

364
00:13:37,651 --> 00:13:40,903
LOVE IS THE BEST MEDICINE.
THAT'S LAUGHTER.

365
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:42,989
WHY DO YOU DO IT?
I DON'T KNOW.

366
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,907
OKAY, ALL RIGHT.

367
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:51,998
NOW, CHANDLER, YOU WANT TO LIVE
WITH MONICA, RIGHT?

368
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:54,668
YEAH, I DO.

369
00:13:54,709 --> 00:13:57,211
AND, MON, YOU WANT TO LIVE
WITH CHANDLER, DON'T YOU?

370
00:13:57,253 --> 00:13:58,421
YES.

371
00:13:58,463 --> 00:14:00,340
GOOD. A VERBAL CONTRACT
IS BINDING

372
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:01,882
IN THE STATE OF NEW YORK.

373
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:14,895
SO, I UNDERSTAND
YOU'RE LOOKING FOR A PLACE.

374
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:18,399
NO, NO, I'M STAYING PUT.

375
00:14:18,441 --> 00:14:19,609
OH.

376
00:14:21,110 --> 00:14:24,572
I WAS GOING TO OFFER YOU
MY APARTMENT.

377
00:14:24,614 --> 00:14:27,367
WHY? WHERE ARE YOU GOING?

378
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:29,952
I DON'T KNOW.

379
00:14:32,163 --> 00:14:33,373
HEY... RACH.

380
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,666
HI.

381
00:14:34,708 --> 00:14:36,668
WELL, YOU'RE NEVER
GOING TO BELIEVE IT.

382
00:14:36,710 --> 00:14:38,961
UM, MONICA AND CHANDLER
ARE MOVING IN AGAIN.

383
00:14:39,003 --> 00:14:40,588
IT'S GREAT NEWS, RIGHT?

384
00:14:40,630 --> 00:14:42,215
I MEAN, FOR THEM, RIGHT?

385
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:43,966
OH, WOW.

386
00:14:44,008 --> 00:14:46,553
YEAH, BUT ON THE
BRIGHT SIDE, WE GET
TO BE ROOMMATES AGAIN.

387
00:14:46,594 --> 00:14:48,680
YE... YEAH.

388
00:14:48,722 --> 00:14:52,266
YOU KNOW, ABOUT THAT, UM...

389
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,935
ROSS, I... I REALLY APPRECIATE
YOUR OFFER

390
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:57,271
TO LET ME MOVE IN
AND EVERYTHING, BUT...

391
00:14:57,313 --> 00:14:59,607
DON'T YOU THINK
IT'S GOING TO BE WEIRD?

392
00:14:59,649 --> 00:15:01,442
WH-WHY?

393
00:15:01,484 --> 00:15:05,446
WHY-WHY WOULD IT--
WHY WOULD IT BE WEIRD?

394
00:15:05,488 --> 00:15:08,491
WELL, YOU KNOW,
BECAUSE OF US--

395
00:15:08,533 --> 00:15:10,660
BECAUSE OF OUR HISTORY.

396
00:15:10,702 --> 00:15:12,245
( high-pitched voice ):
NO!

397
00:15:12,286 --> 00:15:13,621
NO?

398
00:15:13,663 --> 00:15:15,248
NO! NO!

399
00:15:15,289 --> 00:15:16,416
IT WOULD ONLY BE WEIRD

400
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,959
IF WE WERE STILL
IN THAT PLACE.

401
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:22,380
I MEAN, ARE YOU
STILL IN THAT PLACE?

402
00:15:22,422 --> 00:15:23,757
NO, NOT AT ALL.

403
00:15:23,798 --> 00:15:25,007
GOOD. ME NEITHER.

404
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:27,218
SO IT'S NOT A PROBLEM.

405
00:15:27,260 --> 00:15:29,011
AND WE'RE JUST
TWO FRIENDS

406
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:31,138
WHO HAPPEN TO
BE ROOMMATES.

407
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,599
OKAY, BUT, ROSS

408
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,768
EVENTUALLY YOU AND I
ARE GOING TO BE DATING.

409
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:39,731
REALLY. WE ARE.

410
00:15:39,773 --> 00:15:41,649
WELL, YEAH. I'M GOING
TO HAVE A BOYFRIEND

411
00:15:41,691 --> 00:15:43,359
AND YOU'RE GOING
TO HAVE A GIRLFRIEND.

412
00:15:43,401 --> 00:15:45,986
OHH.

413
00:15:46,028 --> 00:15:47,280
THAT'D BE GREAT.

414
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:48,823
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT?

415
00:15:48,865 --> 00:15:50,617
IF YOU THINK
IT'S GOING TO BE OKAY

416
00:15:50,658 --> 00:15:52,326
WE'LL JUST WORK OUT
A SYSTEM.

417
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:54,036
YOU KNOW, IT'LL BE
LIKE IN COLLEGE.

418
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,372
I'LL HANG A HANGER ON THE DOOR
AND PUT A SIGN:

419
00:15:56,414 --> 00:15:57,832
"COME BACK LATER.

420
00:15:57,874 --> 00:15:59,542
I'M GETTING LUCKY."

421
00:16:00,919 --> 00:16:03,170
( cackling )

422
00:16:04,714 --> 00:16:06,633
YEAH, I DIDN'T
THINK OF THAT.

423
00:16:08,635 --> 00:16:12,513
SO ARE YOU SURE ABOUT THIS
WHOLE MOVING IN THING?

424
00:16:12,555 --> 00:16:15,433
I MEAN,
IT'S A REALLY BIG STEP.

425
00:16:15,475 --> 00:16:17,268
AND WHAT'S THE RUSH?

426
00:16:19,145 --> 00:16:21,773
( Chandler and Monica
laughing )

427
00:16:21,815 --> 00:16:23,399
THAT'S VERY FUNNY.

428
00:16:23,441 --> 00:16:25,025
HE'S BEING SILLY
BECAUSE HE KNOWS

429
00:16:25,067 --> 00:16:26,486
THAT WE ENJOY THE SILLINESS.

430
00:16:28,446 --> 00:16:30,239
NO, I'M-I'M
SERIOUS, OKAY?

431
00:16:30,281 --> 00:16:31,699
I MEAN, THINK
ABOUT IT.

432
00:16:31,741 --> 00:16:33,075
YOU MOVE IN

433
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:35,870
UH, YOU START FIGHTING
OVER STUPID GAME ROOMS.

434
00:16:35,912 --> 00:16:37,997
NEXT THING YOU KNOW,
YOU BREAK UP.

435
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:39,457
ROSS, YOU WERE RIGHT BEFORE.

436
00:16:39,499 --> 00:16:41,501
IT WAS JUST A STUPID FIGHT
ABOUT A ROOM.

437
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:43,336
LOOK, THERE ARE
NO STUPID FIGHTS.

438
00:16:44,671 --> 00:16:47,131
THIS ISN'T ABOUT THE ROOM.

439
00:16:47,173 --> 00:16:50,635
THIS IS
ABOUT WHAT THE ROOMREPRESENTS

440
00:16:50,677 --> 00:16:54,973
AND UNFORTUNATELY,
THIS ROOM COULD DESTROY YOU.

441
00:16:55,014 --> 00:16:57,016
YEAH, I'M NOT SO WORRIED.

442
00:16:57,057 --> 00:16:58,643
YEAH. NO, ME NEITHER.

443
00:16:58,685 --> 00:17:00,561
FINE. IT'S YOUR LIFE.

444
00:17:02,146 --> 00:17:04,941
I JUST DON'T WANT TO SEE
YOU GUYS BREAK UP, YOU KNOW?

445
00:17:04,983 --> 00:17:08,152
WHICH YOU WILL DO
IF YOU MOVE IN TOGETHER.

446
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:13,449
BUT IF THAT'S WHAT YOU WANT,
THERE'S NOTHING I CAN DO.

447
00:17:13,491 --> 00:17:14,784
DON'T DO IT!

448
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:22,000
YOU STILL WANT TO MOVE
IN TOGETHER, RIGHT?

449
00:17:22,040 --> 00:17:23,041
OF COURSE.

450
00:17:23,083 --> 00:17:24,669
ROSS DIDN'T SCARE YOU?

451
00:17:24,711 --> 00:17:27,755
SCARED ME OUT OF EVER
WANTING TO LIVE WITH HIM.

452
00:17:27,797 --> 00:17:29,924
HEY, COME HERE.
I GOT TO SHOW YOU SOMETHING.

453
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:31,009
OKAY.

454
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:34,971
OH, MY GOD.

455
00:17:35,013 --> 00:17:37,974
SOMEONE'S KILLED
SQUARE MAN.

456
00:17:38,016 --> 00:17:40,935
THIS IS WHERE I THOUGHT
THE BARCALOUNGER COULD GO.

457
00:17:40,977 --> 00:17:42,812
YOU SEE, YOU
CAN SEE THE TV

458
00:17:42,854 --> 00:17:44,898
AND STILL, IT'S
WALKING DISTANCE
TO THE KITCHEN.

459
00:17:44,939 --> 00:17:46,941
OH, THAT'S SO SWEET.

460
00:17:46,983 --> 00:17:49,193
I WANT TO SHOW
YOU SOMETHING, TOO.
OKAY.

461
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:51,654
YOU KNOW THOSE
BIG, BIG ROAD SIGNS

462
00:17:51,696 --> 00:17:52,989
THAT SAY "MERGE"?

463
00:17:53,031 --> 00:17:53,865
MM-HMM.

464
00:17:53,907 --> 00:17:55,199
YOU KNOW?

465
00:17:55,241 --> 00:17:56,743
SO I WAS THINKING
THAT WE COULD GET

466
00:17:56,784 --> 00:17:58,578
ONE OF THOSE SIGNS
AND HANG IT OVER OUR BED...

467
00:18:00,246 --> 00:18:03,207
BECAUSE
THAT'S YOU AND I TOGETHER.

468
00:18:03,249 --> 00:18:04,500
"MERGE."

469
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,294
OH, MY GOD, I LOVE THAT.

470
00:18:07,336 --> 00:18:08,212
REALLY?

471
00:18:08,254 --> 00:18:09,380
UH, NO.

472
00:18:13,051 --> 00:18:16,512
♪ I FOUND YOU IN MY BED ♪

473
00:18:16,554 --> 00:18:19,223
♪ HOW'D YOU WIND UP THERE? ♪

474
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:22,518
♪ YOU ARE A MYSTERY ♪

475
00:18:22,560 --> 00:18:24,979
♪ LITTLE BLACK CURLY HAIR ♪

476
00:18:25,021 --> 00:18:28,107
♪ LITTLE BLACK CURLY HAIR ♪

477
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:31,402
♪ LITTLE BLACK, LITTLE BLACK,
LITTLE BLACK, LITTLE BLACK ♪

478
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:36,240
♪ LITTLE BLACK CURLY HAIR. ♪

479
00:18:36,282 --> 00:18:37,366
( applause )

480
00:18:37,408 --> 00:18:38,534
THANK YOU.

481
00:18:39,953 --> 00:18:41,621
UM... NOW

482
00:18:41,662 --> 00:18:44,749
IF YOU WANT TO RECEIVE E-MAILS
ABOUT MY UPCOMING SHOWS

483
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:47,919
THEN PLEASE GIVE ME MONEY
SO I CAN BUY A COMPUTER.

484
00:18:50,964 --> 00:18:52,130
SO, UH...

485
00:18:52,172 --> 00:18:53,507
( clearing throat )

486
00:18:53,549 --> 00:18:55,593
WHERE ARE THE OTHER GUYS?
UM, WELL, LET'S SEE.

487
00:18:55,635 --> 00:18:58,220
MONICA AND CHANDLER
ARE OCCUPIED.

488
00:18:58,262 --> 00:18:59,973
FIGHTING?
NO, THE OTHER THING.

489
00:19:01,599 --> 00:19:04,102
I REALLY THINK IT'S GREAT
THEY WORKED THINGS OUT.

490
00:19:04,143 --> 00:19:06,771
YEAH, THERE'S NO BREAKING
THEM UP, IS THERE?

491
00:19:06,813 --> 00:19:08,731
HEY, CAN I BORROW
THE KEY TO YOUR HOUSE

492
00:19:08,773 --> 00:19:11,067
SO I CAN RUN ACROSS THE
STREET AND MAKE A COPY?

493
00:19:11,109 --> 00:19:12,150
SURE. HERE.

494
00:19:12,192 --> 00:19:13,736
THANK YOU.

495
00:19:13,778 --> 00:19:15,404
NOW, ARE YOU SURE?

496
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:18,324
BECAUSE ONCE I MAKE A COPY,
THERE'S NO TURNING BACK.

497
00:19:18,365 --> 00:19:19,826
YEAH, I'M SURE.

498
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:22,745
NOW, GET OUT OF HERE
BEFORE I CHANGE MY MIND.

499
00:19:22,787 --> 00:19:24,455
( Rachel laughing )

500
00:19:26,958 --> 00:19:28,417
UH...

501
00:19:28,459 --> 00:19:30,086
LISTEN, ROSS...
YOU REALLY THINK

502
00:19:30,128 --> 00:19:33,172
THIS MOVING IN WITH RACHEL
IS A GOOD IDEA?

503
00:19:33,213 --> 00:19:35,800
I'VE BEEN BACK AND FORTH.

504
00:19:35,842 --> 00:19:38,469
YEAH, WELL, MAYBE YOU
SHOULD GO BACK, OKAY?

505
00:19:38,511 --> 00:19:40,596
RACHEL MOVES IN
AND, BEFORE YOU KNOW IT

506
00:19:40,638 --> 00:19:42,723
YOU'RE RIGHT WHERE
YOU DON'T WANT TO BE--

507
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:43,850
BACK TOGETHER.

508
00:19:43,891 --> 00:19:45,184
YEAH, I DON'T THINK SO.

509
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,269
SHE'S ALREADY TALKING
ABOUT, YOU KNOW

510
00:19:47,311 --> 00:19:48,354
DATING OTHER GUYS.

511
00:19:48,395 --> 00:19:50,106
THAT'S NOT GOING
TO WORK OUT.

512
00:19:50,148 --> 00:19:52,441
THEN SHE'S GOING
TO COME HOME ALL WEEPY

513
00:19:52,483 --> 00:19:54,944
AND YOU'LL BE TELLING HER,
"OH, THAT'S OKAY.

514
00:19:54,986 --> 00:19:56,154
YOU'LL FIND SOMEONE."

515
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:58,156
AND THEN BAM! SHE FINDS YOU.

516
00:20:00,867 --> 00:20:02,076
WOW...

517
00:20:02,118 --> 00:20:03,536
WELL, MAYBE
YOU'RE RIGHT.

518
00:20:03,577 --> 00:20:05,663
I AM TELLING YOU, ROSS,
SHE IS DEFINITELY GOING

519
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:07,331
TO FALL IN LOVE
WITH YOU AGAIN.

520
00:20:07,373 --> 00:20:08,749
NOW, IS THAT WHAT YOU WANT?

521
00:20:08,791 --> 00:20:10,877
AW, IS THAT WHAT I WANT.

522
00:20:10,918 --> 00:20:12,503
( loudly over microphone):
YES.

523
00:20:15,339 --> 00:20:17,884
OKAY, HOLD ON. I'M GOING
TO MAKE YOUR LIFE MUCH EASIER.

524
00:20:17,925 --> 00:20:19,552
ALL RIGHT, WELL,
THE PLACE WAS CLOSED.

525
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:21,220
I'LL JUST COPY
IT LATER.

526
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:22,638
OR NOT.

527
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,141
WELL, RACH, WHY DON'T
YOU JUST MOVE IN WITH ME?

528
00:20:25,183 --> 00:20:26,684
Ross:
OH, WHOA

529
00:20:26,726 --> 00:20:28,144
WHOA, JOEY.

530
00:20:28,186 --> 00:20:30,479
OH, NO, NO, NO,
NO, NO, NO, IT'S OKAY.

531
00:20:30,521 --> 00:20:33,066
I MEAN, LOOK, RACH,
I KNOW I SCARED YOU OFF

532
00:20:33,107 --> 00:20:36,485
WITH THAT WHOLE
NAKED THURSDAYS THING, BUT...

533
00:20:36,527 --> 00:20:38,988
WE DON'T HAVE TO DO THAT.

534
00:20:39,030 --> 00:20:42,116
WELL... IT WOULD BE EASIER TO
MOVE JUST RIGHT ACROSS THE HALL.

535
00:20:43,201 --> 00:20:44,535
WAIT A MINUTE--

536
00:20:44,577 --> 00:20:47,830
UNLESS YOU'RE THINKING
ABOUT NAKED WEDNESDAYS.

537
00:20:47,872 --> 00:20:50,624
THURSDAY'S CLEARLY
NOT GOOD FOR YOU.

538
00:20:50,666 --> 00:20:51,667
PICK A DAY.

539
00:20:51,709 --> 00:20:53,794
( scoffs )

540
00:20:57,924 --> 00:20:59,383
HI. COME ON IN.
HI.

541
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:00,634
THANKS FOR
COMING BACK.

542
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:02,136
UM, THERE'VE BEEN
A LOT OF PEOPLE

543
00:21:02,178 --> 00:21:04,388
INTERESTED IN THE ROOM,
BUT I HAVE NARROWED IT DOWN

544
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:05,806
AND YOU ARE ONE
OF THE FINALISTS.

545
00:21:05,848 --> 00:21:08,017
GREAT.

546
00:21:08,059 --> 00:21:10,436
OKAY, NOW,
BEFORE I MAKE MY DECISION

547
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:11,687
I JUST WANT TO MAKE SURE

548
00:21:11,729 --> 00:21:13,480
THAT OUR PERSONALITIES
MATCH, OKAY?

549
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:14,899
SO I MADE UP A LITTLE TEST.

550
00:21:14,941 --> 00:21:16,400
NOW, I'M GOING TO SAY A WORD

551
00:21:16,442 --> 00:21:19,070
AND THEN YOU SAY THE FIRST
THING THAT COMES TO MIND.

552
00:21:19,112 --> 00:21:20,487
I CAN DO THAT.

553
00:21:20,529 --> 00:21:21,864
OKAY, HERE WE GO.

554
00:21:21,906 --> 00:21:22,865
PILLOW.

555
00:21:22,907 --> 00:21:24,575
FIGHT.

556
00:21:24,617 --> 00:21:25,618
VERY GOOD.

557
00:21:27,453 --> 00:21:28,662
"G."

558
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:31,040
STRING?
EXCELLENT.

559
00:21:31,082 --> 00:21:33,126
OKAY

560
00:21:33,167 --> 00:21:35,253
UM...

561
00:21:35,293 --> 00:21:36,921
DOGGIE.

562
00:21:36,963 --> 00:21:39,090
KITTEN?

563
00:21:39,132 --> 00:21:41,341
OOH, SORRY.

564
00:21:41,383 --> 00:21:42,885
( making irritated
sound )

565
00:21:42,927 --> 00:21:45,221
NO, NO, SO CLOSE, THOUGH
BUT, YOU KNOW, OKAY, BYE-BYE.

566
00:21:45,263 --> 00:21:48,348
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

